== M3 RC100 native route: Newtonian-floor fraction vs z (CFG303 per-galaxy CSV) ==
N inverted 59 | floor (f <= 0.02) 41
   {'z': '0.5-1.0', 'n': 26, 'floor': 7, 'frac': 0.27, 'median_log_a0_censored': -9.797, 'median_log_a0_inverted_only': -9.578}
   {'z': '1.0-1.5', 'n': 18, 'floor': 6, 'frac': 0.33, 'median_log_a0_censored': -9.984, 'median_log_a0_inverted_only': -9.658}
   {'z': '1.5-2.0', 'n': 15, 'floor': 7, 'frac': 0.47, 'median_log_a0_censored': -10.122, 'median_log_a0_inverted_only': -9.684}
   {'z': '2.0-2.6', 'n': 41, 'floor': 21, 'frac': 0.51, 'median_log_a0_censored': None, 'median_log_a0_inverted_only': -9.732}
Spearman(z, floor) = +0.249 (p 0.013);  Spearman(z, log a0) inverted only = -0.158 (p 0.231);  with the floor discs ranked lowest = -0.274 (p 0.0057)
Reading: the floor fraction rises with z (27% -> 51%); excluding floor discs removes the low-a0 tail preferentially at high z. With the censoring kept, the native implied a0 FALLS with z -- inconsistent with all three laws, i.e. a z-dependent bias of the native baryons, which the paper's own decision rule ('inconsistent with all of them counts against all of them') would read as a calibration failure.

